From 64695e8df3f035548d083539aa91274ac38526d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blue898 <201240079+blue898@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:49:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 138/146] Input: max77693-haptic: stop at 61/64 of the PWM
 period

At magnitudes of about 240 of 255 and above (Android's ringtone
vibration runs at full strength) the duty cycle came out at 100 %.
pwm-samsung then writes TCMPB = 0xffffffff and the output is a constant
level. The MAX77693 takes the LRA's drive frequency from the edges of
the external PWM: without edges the motor only hums. Lower magnitudes
vibrated normally at 201 Hz.

Scale the duty cycle to 61/64 of the period at full magnitude, 97.7 %,
which is what Samsung's vendor driver uses (37050 of 37904 ns).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/misc/max77693-haptic.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/max77693-haptic.c b/drivers/input/misc/max77693-haptic.c
index 5d45680d7..357d9fdcc 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/max77693-haptic.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/max77693-haptic.c
@@ -257,8 +257,14 @@ static int max77693_haptic_play_effect(struct input_dev *dev, void *data,
 	 */
 	pwm_get_args(haptic->pwm_dev, &pargs);
 	period_mag_multi = (u64)pargs.period * haptic->magnitude;
-	haptic->pwm_duty = (unsigned int)(period_mag_multi >>
-						MAX_MAGNITUDE_SHIFT);
+	/*
+	 * Stop at 61/64 of the period, a duty cycle of 97.7 % at full magnitude like
+	 * Samsung's vendor driver (37050 of 37904 ns). The MAX77693 takes the LRA's
+	 * drive frequency from the edges of the external PWM: at 100 % there are none
+	 * left and the motor only hums.
+	 */
+	haptic->pwm_duty = (unsigned int)((period_mag_multi * 61) >>
+						(MAX_MAGNITUDE_SHIFT + 6));
 
 	schedule_work(&haptic->work);
 
